     "<div dir=\"auto\"><div>Hi John. I haven&#39;t used Presence for awhile so I may not be accurately interpreting your question, but my initial hunch is that you might want to use Julian day as a continuous covariate to parameterize within-season temporal effects, and some categorical covariate to represent among-season/year effects. I&#39;m not clear on what model you&#39;re attempting to use, though, and you&#39;ll probably get much smarter answers than this but here&#39;s a start.</div><div dir=\"auto\"><br></div><div dir=\"auto\">PS, post an example of your code.<br><br><div data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\" dir=\"auto\">Matt Giovanni<br><a href=\"tel:(608)%20320-9331\" value=\"+16083209331\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">608-320-9331</a></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\" dir=\"auto\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div></div>"
